# rmb-desktop releases

When the user asks to cut, ship, publish, or deploy a release — or when a fix is ready for the remote instance — **run the release pipeline yourself**. Do not ask permission to upload to GitHub.

Versioning: see `plan/parallel-work-and-versioning.md` §3. **`Makefile` `VERSION ?=` is the single source of truth.** The Tauri-era version files (`app/package.json`, `app/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`) were deleted in Phase 4 — do not resurrect them.

## One command

```bash
cd /Users/liguanghui/Virginia/colinleefish/rmb-desktop
SIGN_KEYCHAIN_PASS='rmb-sign' make release VERSION=0.2.x
```

Or upload an already-built DMG:

```bash
UPLOAD_ONLY=1 make release VERSION=0.2.x
```

Credentials live in `~/.rmb/release.env` (see `scripts/release.env.example`). Prefer sourcing that file over prompting.

## Pipeline (automatic, since 0.2.0)

1. `make build-all VERSION=X` — webui build + Go build (`bin/{rmb-app,rmb,rmbd}`)
2. `make sidecar-bundles VERSION=X` — cross-built sidecar tarballs/zip + ed25519-signed `dist/manifest.json`
3. `make app-build VERSION=X` — hand-rolled `.app` bundle (not Tauri) + codesign + DMG
4. `make notarize` — Apple notarization + staple (skip with `SKIP_NOTARIZE=1`)
5. `scripts/release.sh X` — verify staple, upload DMG + sidecar bundles + signed manifest to GitHub, then `PUBLISH_R2=1` pushes `latest.json`/`versions.json` + bundles to `releases.re-mem-ber.me` (China primary feed)

## Version bumps

Before releasing, update `VERSION` in:
- `Makefile` (default `VERSION ?=`) — **single source of truth**

Commit the version bump only when the user asks. The updater never auto-installs prereleases (`-rc.N`); staging feeds must use prerelease suffixes.

## After upload

- Confirm release URL: `https://github.com/colinleefish/rmb-desktop/releases/tag/vX.Y.Z`
- Confirm feed: `curl https://releases.re-mem-ber.me/latest.json` (must equal X.Y.Z, signature verifiable)
- Remote test host (`10.254.24.7:19019`): user installs DMG manually unless they ask you to deploy via SSH
